# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list for the opensign-server image
# (used via --ignorefile in .github/workflows/opensign-server-rebuild.yml).
#
# WHY THESE ARE ACCEPTED
# The OS layer is NOT ignored: the Dockerfile runs `apt-get dist-upgrade`
# (refreshed every time the base image digest moves -- see
# .opensign-server-base-digest), so the Debian packages + LibreOffice ship at
# their latest point-release and the only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH findings left
# in the image are the Node.js application + npm dependencies below. Every one
# is either baked into the pinned node:22.14.0 image (the npm CLI's own
# transitive tree) or pinned by upstream's apps/OpenSignServer/package-lock.json,
# and each has a newer version on the npm registry that fixes it -- we just
# can't move it without forking OpenSign's dependency tree or floating the
# pinned node:22.14.0 base, both of which this repo deliberately avoids for
# reproducibility.
#
# The fixable CRITICAL findings in this image are tar (CVE-2026-59873, in the
# npm CLI's bundled tree). OpenSign v3.0.0 bumped proxy-addr / @grpc/grpc-js /
# axios / sharp / undici / js-yaml / multer past their advisories, so those
# ids were pruned on 2026-11-02 (the old lodash / marked / minimist /
# underscore ones went on 2026-10-10).

# Lower severities and CVEs with no available fix are reported by Trivy but
# don't block; only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH do (trivy-scan.sh), so a fresh CVE
# in the OS layer or a dependency bump will fail the build until it's either
# patched or explicitly added here with a reason.
#
# Re-check after a node:22.14.0 -> node:X.Y.Z base bump and after each
# OpenSign release: a newer node bundles a newer npm (shrinking the
# node-bundled set) and upstream may have bumped proxy-addr / axios / multer.
# Prune ids Trivy no longer reports (stale entries would silently hide a
# regression back to a vulnerable version).

# --- node:22.14.0's bundled npm (the npm CLI's own dependency tree) --------
# brace-expansion 2.0.1
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# glob 10.4.5
CVE-2025-64756

# ip-address 9.0.5
CVE-2026-69192

# minimatch 9.0.5
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# pacote 19.0.1 + 20.0.0
CVE-2026-9496

# sigstore 3.0.0
CVE-2026-48815

# tar 6.2.1 + 7.4.3
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566

# --- apps/OpenSignServer dependency tree (OpenSign v3.0.0) -------------------
# Pinned by upstream's package-lock.json (or resolved by its plain
# `npm install`); each fix is waiting on an upstream OpenSign dep bump (or a
# lockfile override, which this repo deliberately avoids).
#
# @graphql-tools/utils 10.11.0 + 9.2.1 (GraphQL layer; prototype pollution in
# mergeDeep / mergeIncrementalResult)
CVE-2026-104852
CVE-2026-114604

# body-parser 2.3.0 (express request parsing; DoS via decompression error)
CVE-2026-111181

# follow-redirects 1.16.1 (axios transitive; cross-origin info disclosure)
CVE-2026-116689

# multer 2.4.0 (file-upload surface; DoS via aborted request)
CVE-2026-113872

# node-forge 1.4.0 (signing-certificate / PKCS#12 handling; TLS-record DoS
# and parser issues)
CVE-2026-118779
CVE-2026-118782
CVE-2026-119187
CVE-2026-119188
CVE-2026-119190

# nodemailer 9.1.1 (SMTP outbound; DoS via crafted headers / quadratic
# complexity)
CVE-2026-90776
GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j
